WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:02.580
MINHAZ KAZI: Welcome
to "Data Vis Dev Talk."

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.590
I'm your host, Minhaz Kazi.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.300
In this video
series, we will talk

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.820
about Google's next-generation
business intelligence

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.060
and dashboarding
tool, Data Studio.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.850
We will also show how you
can build your own connector

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:18.820
to connect to any data source
and then visualize that data.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.530
Data Studio is a simple-to-use
yet powerful reporting tool

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.720
that can be used for free.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.590
It is completely web-based,
so users can create and view

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.860
beautiful dashboards using
their browser regardless of what

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.800
operating system they're on.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:36.120
The dynamic and interactive
nature of Data Studio

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.820
ensures that users are
always getting the updated

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:43.710
information when visualizing and
interactively exploring data.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.590
Developers also get a lot of
flexibility building solutions

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:48.990
around Data Studio
since it works well

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.370
with other Google Cloud Platform
and Google Marketing Platform

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.710
tools.

00:00:53.710 --> 00:00:55.650
In this video, we
will briefly talk

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.170
about how Data Studio works
and who can benefit from it.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:00.118
Let's get started.

00:01:00.118 --> 00:01:02.558
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:04.998 --> 00:01:09.010
Let's think of a few use cases
for data visualization first.

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:11.430
Maybe you are a developer
who have an existing

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.130
product or service and are
looking to build a developer

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.270
solution on top of it.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:18.900
You plan to make this solution
available to all your users

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.160
in a cost-effective way.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:24.390
Or maybe you're an analyst
at an organization trying

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:28.170
to monitor internal KPIs like
sales, or inventory data,

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:31.140
or have your own
balance scorecard.

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.500
As an executive, you
might need an easy to use

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.040
yet visually pleasing tool
to talk about last quarter's

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.180
growth in an all-hands meeting.

00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:42.990
Data storytelling helps
people to understand insights

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.520
from a data set.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:48.090
Journalists need tools to
make the technical parts easy

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:50.340
and let them focus on the
insights and storytelling

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.510
parts.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.880
As a researcher, you
might need a platform

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.220
to visually analyze
your research data

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.670
and then publish the findings
in an interactive blog.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.950
Or maybe you are the
owner of a unique data set

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:03.780
and would like to
visualize and share

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.100
that data set with others.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.280
In each of these
use cases, it helps

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.880
to have a solution that
is, one, scalable--

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:15.210
it works even if a large
number of people are using it--

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:19.500
two, interactive-- it's not just
a screenshot or static content.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.050
Users should be able to
tweak, adjust, change

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:25.180
settings and filters to
derive their own conclusions--

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.320
three, cost-effective-- it
should not break the bank

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.990
or take up massive amounts of
time for developers to build

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.670
and maintain the solution--

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.530
and four, high-performing--
the solution

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:38.730
should work fast and respond
quickly to user interactions

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.920
even with gigabytes of data.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.020
Data Studio can help
you to build solutions

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.480
with all four criteria.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.820
Data Studio makes
life easier for users,

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.700
enabling them to organize,
access, and understand

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.956
their world of information.

00:02:52.956 --> 00:02:55.080
So let's see how
Data Studio works.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.530
There are four steps to it--

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:00.660
connect, analyze,
visualize, and share.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:03.420
First, you connect your
data in Data Studio.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.200
Your data can be in
different places.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.110
Data Studio provides
different connectors

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:09.420
to let you connect to your data.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.690
We'll talk more about this
connect step in our next video.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.325
Next comes the analyze
and visualize part.

00:03:15.325 --> 00:03:17.200
I like to combine these
two steps, since they

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.740
are highly related and
depend on each other.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:23.820
Data Studio provides different
features for these two steps.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:27.650
You can use Data Studio Explorer
to visually explore the data.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:30.270
Data Blending lets you blend
data from multiple sources

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.550
into one single
data source based

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:35.550
on a single field
or a composite key.

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:37.410
You can always do
manual calculations

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:40.770
and create custom fields
using different functions.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:42.930
When it comes to
visualizations, Data Studio

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.340
comes with a number of
built-in chart types,

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.380
including bar, column,
line, time series, scatter,

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.570
et cetera.

00:03:50.570 --> 00:03:54.390
You can also have data tables,
pivot tables, and scorecards.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:57.060
There are custom templates
available in the report gallery

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:59.280
that can get you
started quickly.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.160
Also, if you have need for a
specific type of visualization

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:05.790
and it is not available, you can
develop your own visualization

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:09.420
using JavaScript
libraries like D3.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.060
Once you have built and
started using your dashboard,

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.990
you can share it with others.

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:16.649
Sharing works using the
Google Drive permissions.

00:04:16.649 --> 00:04:20.279
You can provide view are edit
access to certain people using

00:04:20.279 --> 00:04:22.620
their emails or email groups.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.960
You can always
share using a link.

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:27.330
If you share edit
access with others,

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.250
multiple people can
work collaboratively

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:33.390
on the same dashboard,
just like Google Docs.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.700
You can take your
dashboard link and embed it

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.954
in your website or blog post
using IFrames or oEmbed.

00:04:39.954 --> 00:04:42.120
Viewers of your site will
be able to see the updated

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:45.900
data on the dashboard and
interact it on your site.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:47.880
You can also use your
dashboard as a slide deck

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:51.550
when presenting insights
and findings to an audience.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.120
So that was an overview
of how Data Studio works

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.830
and who can benefit from it.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.960
In our next video,
we'll talk about how

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.850
you can connect to your
own data in Data Studio.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:02.722
You can always go to
our developer site

00:05:02.722 --> 00:05:05.890
at
developers.google.com/datastudio

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.280
for more information.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.030
Thanks for watching.

